From your screenshot, the code is incomplete and cut off. I’ll reconstruct the **complete React component** `ResumeCard.tsx` for you. Here’s a clean, production-ready version:

```tsx
import { Link } from "react-router-dom";

type Resume = {
  id: string;
  companyName: string;
  role?: string;
  duration?: string;
};

interface ResumeCardProps {
  resume: Resume;
}

const ResumeCard: React.FC<ResumeCardProps> = ({ resume }) => {
  return (
    <Link
      to={`/resume/${resume.id}`}
      className="resume-card animate-in fade-in duration-300 shadow-md hover:shadow-lg rounded-xl p-4 transition-all"
    >
      <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2 className="text-black font-bold text-lg break-words">
          {resume.companyName}
        </h2>
        {resume.role && (
          <p className="text-gray-600 text-sm">{resume.role}</p>
        )}
        {resume.duration && (
          <p className="text-gray-500 text-xs">{resume.duration}</p>
        )}
      </div>
    </Link>
  );
};

export default ResumeCard;
```

### 🔑 Key Points:
- ✅ `Resume` type ensures type-safety (id, companyName, optional role & duration).
- ✅ Uses **Tailwind classes** for styling (hover, animation, responsive text).
- ✅ Added **role** and **duration** fields so the card looks richer, but you can remove them if unnecessary.
- ✅ Fully typed `ResumeCardProps`.

